# Auto-rebuild rule (iOS, physical iPad or iPhone)

After any non-doc code change, rebuild and install on a connected physical device. Prefer iPad (this app is iPad-first); fall back to a connected iPhone. If neither is connected, STOP — do not target any simulator. The user starts simulators manually. Skip for doc-only or `.cursor/**` changes.

This repo lives under a file-provider dir (`code.nosync`). Build to a derived-data path OUTSIDE that tree or codesign will fail with "resource fork, Finder information, or similar detritus not allowed".

Run from the repo root:

```bash
DD="$HOME/Library/Developer/Xcode/DerivedData/VibeWMiOS-auto"

# Extract a UUID-shaped UDID from `devicectl list devices` output.
# `{print $NF}` no longer works — recent devicectl puts the product id (e.g. `(iPhone15,3)`)
# in the last column, so we grep the UUID column by regex instead.
pick_udid() {
  local match="$1" # "ipad" or "iphone"
  xcrun devicectl list devices 2>/dev/null \
    | awk -v m="$match" 'tolower($0) ~ m && /connected/ {
        for (i=1; i<=NF; i++)
          if ($i ~ /^[A-F0-9]{8}-[A-F0-9]{4}-[A-F0-9]{4}-[A-F0-9]{4}-[A-F0-9]{12}$/) { print $i; exit }
      }'
}

UDID=$(pick_udid ipad)
if [ -z "$UDID" ]; then UDID=$(pick_udid iphone); fi
if [ -z "$UDID" ]; then
  echo "no physical iPad or iPhone connected - aborting auto-rebuild (do NOT target a simulator)"
  exit 1
fi
echo "auto-rebuild target UDID=$UDID"

xcodebuild -project VibeWindowManagerIOS.xcodeproj \
  -scheme VibeWindowManagerIOS -configuration Debug \
  -destination "id=$UDID" \
  -derivedDataPath "$DD" build
```

On success, install and launch:

```bash
APP="$DD/Build/Products/Debug-iphoneos/VibeWindowManagerIOS.app"
xcrun devicectl device install app --device "$UDID" "$APP"
xcrun devicectl device process launch --device "$UDID" \
  com.thomasguntenaar.VibeWindowManagerIOS
```

Note: `Debug-iphoneos` is correct for both iPad and iPhone device builds — it's the device platform folder, not an iPhone-specific one.

Rules:
- If build fails with "resource fork, Finder information, or similar detritus": confirm derivedDataPath is NOT under `code.nosync`. Never build to `./build` here.
- If build fails because the device OS is older than the deployment target, stop and tell the user which device is too old — do not silently pick another destination.
- If build fails for other reasons, print the first real error and stop. Do not retry blindly.
- Do NOT target a simulator. If no physical iPad or iPhone is connected, stop and tell the user. The user will start simulators manually when needed.
- Do not open Xcode.
- Do not run this for doc-only, README, or `.cursor/**` edits.
